{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the situation carefully.\n\nI need to implement Stage B of B-0035: initial complete inventory and lifecycle in the repository/navigation composition.\n\nKey requirements:\n1. The first `RepositoryCodingHost` model request contains exactly one complete authorized resource inventory as distinct metadata.\n2. Use the accepted `complete_inventory` representation from navigation.py (Stage A).\n3. All resources must have correct addresses, UTF-8 sizes, content identities, and editable flags.\n4. Repository and snapshot IDs must match current observed scope.\n5. The complete inventory is NOT the ranked/incomplete task-candidate view - both must coexist when task navigation is enabled.\n6. Repeated prepare calls don't accumulate duplicate inventory.\n7. After an admitted source change is installed, the next request's inventory describes that current scope.\n8. Inventory does not disclose source text, unauthorized paths, or absolute roots.\n9. Count complete inventory in full serialized ModelRequest capacity.\n10. Keep initial metadata and installed-source refresh behavior available without requiring optional task navigation.\n\nLet me understand the current flow:\n- `prepare()` calls `prepare_navigation()` which appends a task_entry message when policy is not None and len(messages) == 1.\n- `build_request()` assembles the ModelRequest with tools.\n- The inventory needs to be added as a separate metadata message (distinct from the objective).\n\nLooking at the test assertions:\n```python\ndef assert_metadata(data, host):\n    assert data[\"repository_id\"] == str(host.scope.snapshot.repository_id)\n    assert data[\"snapshot_id\"] == str(host.scope.snapshot.id)\n    assert data[\"source_acquired\"] is False\n    rows = {row[\"address\"]: row for row in data[\"resources\"]}\n    assert set(rows) == {\"package/source.py\", \"README.md\"}\n    assert rows[\"package/source.py\"][\"editable\"] is True\n    assert rows[\"README.md\"][\"editable\"] is False\n    for resource in host.scope.snapshot.resources:\n        row = rows[resource.address.value]\n        assert row[\"content_identity\"] == str(resource.content_identity)\n        assert row[\"byte_size\"] == len(resource.content.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n```\n\nSo the test expects `complete_inventory` data to be present in the request. Let me look at how the test extracts it - I need to see more of the focused test file.\n\nLet me think about where to put the inventory:\n- It should be a separate message (distinct metadata) in the messages list.\n- It should be added during `prepare()` or `build_request()`.\n- It should NOT be duplicated on repeated prepare calls.\n- After `apply()`, the scope changes, so the next prepare should reflect the new scope.\n\nThe key constraint: repository.py has only 737 bytes of headroom. navigation.py has substantial space and already owns metadata presentation.\n\nSo I need to:\n1. In navigation.py: add a function that creates/refreshes the inventory message (or modify `prepare_navigation` to also handle inventory).\n2. In repository.py: make minimal changes to wire it up.\n\nLet me think about the design:\n\nOption A: Add a new function in navigation.py like `prepare_inventory` that:\n- Takes messages, scope, editable addresses, and a max_bytes budget\n- Checks if an inventory message already exists (by some marker)\n- If not, or if the snapshot has changed, inserts/replaces the inventory message at position 1 (after the objective)\n\nOption B: Modify `prepare_navigation` to also handle inventory.\n\nGiven the constraint that repository.py has only 737 bytes of headroom, I should put most logic in navigation.py.\n\nLet me think about what \"distinct metadata\" means - it's a separate PromptMessage with a specific format. Looking at how task_entry is used:\n```python\nmessages.append(\n    PromptMessage(\n        \"user\",\n        json.dumps(task_entry(index, objective, policy), ensure_ascii=False),\n    ),\n)\n```\n\nSo the inventory would similarly be a JSON-serialized message. But it needs to be \"distinct\" from the task navigation entry.\n\nLet me look at what the test expects. The test calls `assert_metadata(data, host)` where `data` is presumably extracted from the request messages. Let me read more of the focused test to understand how it extracts the metadata.\n\nLet me read the focused test file to understand the expected structure better.\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_source","arguments":"{\"path\":\"experiments/local_maintenance_task_navigation/focused.py\",\"start\":0,\"end\":4591}"},"id":"Ay1dWYqZOn0aW8dGbpnSq6afaWiIlCax"},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_source","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/devtools/agents/coding/navigation.py\",\"start\":0,\"end\":3625}"},"id":"HuYgtQbRyO76JcNiMFBmZE8L3gOPU8ec"}]}}],"created":1793384436,"model":"qwen38-local","system_fingerprint":"b10868-304665fe7","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1065,"prompt_tokens":7986,"total_tokens":9051,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-cbgd9sAtV2rDYTM1T1Nl6CDfl5cbME9m","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":7986,"prompt_ms":8777.594,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0991227147508138,"prompt_per_second":909.8165169179618,"predicted_n":1065,"predicted_ms":46490.387,"predicted_per_token_ms":43.693972744360906,"predicted_per_second":22.886451773352626}}